<span id="glance-title" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"></span><span
  id="glance-close-title"
  class="anchor-alias"
  aria-hidden="true"></span>
<section
  class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top"
  aria-labelledby="glance-section-0"
>
  <div>
    <h2
      id="glance-section-0"
    >
      Bring another open tab into view.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Choose explicitly</h3><p>
        Press ⌘⇧G on macOS or Ctrl+Shift+G on Windows and Linux, or choose View
        → Open Glance. Pick a tab from the current window; the picker stays
        within its local profile.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Put it where you want it</h3><p>
        Drag the card’s header to move it, or an edge to resize it, or use the
        arrow keys on its Move or resize control. Double-click the header to
        put it back. Blanc remembers where you left it on this device.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Change, open, or finish</h3><p>
        Use Change to choose another tab, Open as tab to make it the current
        tab, or Keep as split to show the two side by side in Split View. Close
        Glance, or press Escape on its header, without closing either tab.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="glance-section-1">
  <div>
    <h2 id="glance-section-1">
      A temporary view for the task in front of you.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Both visible pages stay available</h3><p>
        Selecting a quiet tab for Glance reloads it. While it is open in Glance,
        Quiet Tabs leaves it alone. The page behind the card stays usable, and
        switching to another tab closes Glance.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Keep the choice local</h3><p>
        The picker uses tabs from this window and profile. It does not search
        history, Favorites, remote tabs, or another window.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="glance-note-title">
  <h2 id="glance-note-title">
    Glance is temporary.
  </h2>
  <p>
    Glance is never written to session restore or sync. Only the card’s size
    and place are remembered, on this device. The underlying ordinary tabs keep
    their usual browsing behavior.
  </p>
  <a
    class="text-link"
    href="/support#tab-groups"
    data-track="feature_cta_click"
    data-feature="glance"
    data-cta-position="related-feature"
    >Keep related tabs in Named Groups <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
  >
</aside>
